{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1520986-bite-damage","id":1520986,"title":"Bite Damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-19T15:08:13-07:00","id":1520986,"title":"Bite Damage","content":"Specifically for Humans, Homids, and Homids with fangs.<br /> <br /> There is no damage listed. Yet, Humans bite. They can bit off fingers. A human bite can kill. But it's not listed as lethal damage. I doubt it's aggravated. Then you have ananasi who have fangs in homid form, but don't do agg damage with their bites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T15:09:59-07:00","id":1520987,"title":"","content":"I believe it's usually given as Strength +1 unless otherwise specified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T15:19:07-07:00","id":1520988,"title":"","content":"Strength+1A, for every supernatural form. But normal homid? Is it bashing or lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T16:16:42-07:00","id":1520993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1520986-bite-damage?p=1520988#post1520988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength+1A, for every supernatural form. But normal homid? Is it bashing or lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might just be Strength bashing. I realize that sounds dumb, but this is the same system where a stone sphere the size of a Crinos head on a long pole does bashing damage when you smash someone with it, even though a Crinos fist is noted as being lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T20:08:18-07:00","id":1521005,"title":"","content":"The most common rule (since this is in the general forum, not the WtA one) is that human bites are Str - 1 bashing, and require a grapple to achieve. Yes, bites can kill, but so can lots of things. The game isn't always realistic, or at least is aiming for things like are possible but rare to be rare by making it statistically very difficult to do.<br /> <br /> Any changes to this would need to be specified by the books.<br /> <br /> For homid shifters with near-human forms (not all of them have one) they can bite without a grapple at diff 8, but for lethal damage (the damage rules get complicated when you take Breeds into account in WtA). So, for a homid Garou:<br /> <br /> Homid: grapple to bite, bashing damage, making it basically cosmetic.<br /> Glabro: +2 diff, Str - 1 lethal damage.<br /> Crinos: Str + 1 aggravated damage.<br /> Hispo: Str + 2 aggravated damage.<br /> Lupus: Str + 1 aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Like, I said, it gets complicated with WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T20:31:28-07:00","id":1521006,"title":"","content":"I would say those are Bashing. Bashing damage is any damage that heals fairly quickly. Those lost health levels can come back in hours. Most human bite damage is fairly superficial breaking of the skin that only requires some anti-septic and bandages. Bashing damage only needs medical treatment if the level is Mauled or worse. Yes, humans can bite off fingers. But that happens only rarely. That is not a typical result - and humans do not naturally attack with our mouths. It is a very exceptional result. Bite attacks really only work once someone is already subdued because someone leading with their face is going to be punched hard in that face. If you want to simulate those very rare human biting off fingers and such, it's best done when the damage rolls have a lot of successes, probably critical hits. Body parts being cut off is not something the combat system handles well - swords can cut off hands and arms, but that is not what actually happens in WoD combat unless special maneuvers and stuff are done.<br /> <br /> Lethal damage is damage that always requires medical treatment before it can heal. That is obviously not most human bite damage. And damage types should not be based on the exceedingly rare exceptions. I could be persuaded that an Ananasi homid breed form that has actual fangs does Lethal damage instead, otherwise why mention they have fangs? It is probably not meant as solely a flavor text description.<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage is essentially the same as Lethal damage except that it is harder to heal by supernatural means. To a human, there is no difference between lethal and aggravated damage. I don't think any supernatural creature is going to have trouble healing human bite damage at all, and that includes Ananasi homid breed form that has fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T19:37:42-07:00","id":1521095,"title":"","content":"I know I've seen descriptions under some Thaumaturgy rituals where cutting off a finger doesn't result in the loss of a Health Level \u2014it's regarded as painful, but not an injury that actually causes peril or lessens the ability to withstand subsequent injury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T01:10:30-07:00","id":1521107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1520986-bite-damage?p=1521006#post1521006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lethal damage is damage that always requires medical treatment before it can heal. That is obviously not most human bite damage. And damage types should not be based on the exceedingly rare exceptions. I could be persuaded that an Ananasi homid breed form that has actual fangs does Lethal damage instead, otherwise why mention they have fangs? It is probably not meant as solely a flavor text description.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dangerous thing (for mortals) and bite wounds is that they tend to easily infect due to the bacteria in the saliva. There's about a 25% chance for a non-superficial bite wound to become infected, but most supernatural beings have enough resistance or immunity to ignore this. As an optional rule, a high success roll on a bite attack could bump the damage type from Bashing to Lethal.<br /> <br /> For the Ananasi, there is the Level 2 Gift <i>Hand Fangs</i> that deals Strength+0 Aggravated damage which I used also for the vanilla bite in Homid form. The more annoying rule is that they can also inject venom in Homid, but with decreased potency - and like all things Ananasi venom, there isn't really any guideline for it. I used the Nagah venom as base for Pithus (7A damage) and then go -1 for every form closer to Homid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T04:17:02-07:00","id":1521120,"title":"","content":"You don't even have to narrow that to bites: infection is one of the most dangerous aspects of any serious injury. Spreading infections are how mosquitos kill over a million people a year. Infections have killed more soldiers than immediate death from weapon wounds.<br /> <br /> It's also something that's just... exceedingly difficult to model in a fun way for games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T07:32:32-07:00","id":1521129,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and I usually handwave this, too. Having a PC drop out of action for a few weeks because they stepped on a rusty nail isn't exactly fun for the player, and having gone through a sepsis I can vouch it isn't for the character either. Bites may warrant an exception because a) there are many bitey things in the WOD and b) even given the best outside conditions, unless the attacker was kind enough to do an antiseptic mouthwash before, bites are a special kind of nasty in this regard. I vaguely remember it being a deliberate thing for some Fomori, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}